  contentsAnswer: Some books and my uncle's old radio. He listens to the same station
    every morning.
  weightAnswer: Ten or eleven kilos. Most of the weight is books.
  metalAnswer: The radio has a metal cover. The rest is paper and cloth.
  packingAnswer: The radio is loose. Unplugged, batteries out. No motor or wound
    mechanism.
  responseAnswer: It can knock once against the books. There should not be another
    movement after the first knock.
  authorReasoning: 'Carrier with a plausible cover: 10.5 kg and modest metal fit.
    The pulse produces delayed sustained corrective movement, contradicting a passive
    loose radio with no powered/wound source. No tilt test required.'
